(### Banner Fields) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `L1%`, `L2%`, `L3%` are percent widths of the HTF range.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `HighBreach` is cumulative per-period high-breach state shown as `1/0`.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `LowBreach` is cumulative per-period low-breach state shown as `1/0`.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `Zone` uses the implemented encoding `10 / 1 / 2 / 3 / -10`.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `ClosePosition` is the normalized HTF close location metric described below.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(## 13. HTF Close Position Metric) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Store where the current LTF close sits inside the HTF range assuming:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `0 = PL`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `100 = PH`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- If close is above `PH`, store `101`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- If close is below `PL`, store `-101`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Saturation is applied regardless of how far outside the range the close is.) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(## 14. Nearest-Level Distance Metrics) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Store the actual distance in ticks from the current close to the two nearest structural levels.) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- For closes above `PH`:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- both `d1` and `d2` equal `abs\(close - PH\)` in ticks) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- For closes below `PL`:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- both `d1` and `d2` equal `abs\(close - PL\)` in ticks) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- For closes inside the HTF range:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `d1` and `d2` are the distances to the two boundaries of the containing zone) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
(## 15. Width Metrics In Ticks) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- Store each level width in ticks:) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `L1 width ticks`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `L2 width ticks`) Tj
0 -14 Td
(- `L3 width ticks`) Tj
0 -14 Td
() Tj
0 -14 Td
